<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis-Gustave Binger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1856">1856</a>–<a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis-Gustave Binger was a French officer and explorer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>. Between 1887 and 1889 he travelled from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-bend">Niger bend</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-guinea">Gulf of Guinea</a> by way of Kong, signing treaties that extended French influence in the interior. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Ivory Coast</a> became a French colony in 1893 he was appointed its first governor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-gustave-binger.jpg" alt="Louis-Gustave Binger" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antoine Meyer, Colmar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gustave_Binger.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
